<DocsLayout title="Introduction">
  <h1>Identity</h1>
  <p>A standalone authentication and user-management service. Deploys as a single container, points at an EntDB instance, exposes Connect-RPC over HTTP/JSON, and ships JWTs that downstream services verify via JWKS.</p>

  <h2>What Identity gives you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email + password</strong> &mdash; signup, login, change, lockout, recovery-email reset</li>
    <li><strong>Passkeys (WebAuthn)</strong> &mdash; registration and login flows</li>
    <li><strong>TOTP 2FA</strong> &mdash; setup, verify, recovery codes, regenerate</li>
    <li><strong>OAuth login</strong> &mdash; Google and Microsoft (server consumes pre-verified tokens)</li>
    <li><strong>QR cross-device login</strong> &mdash; new device proves itself via an already-signed-in device</li>
    <li><strong>Sessions</strong> &mdash; list, revoke, sign-out-everywhere; refresh tokens rotated on every use</li>
    <li><strong>JWT issuance</strong> &mdash; RS256 with key rotation, plus <code>/.well-known/jwks.json</code></li>
    <li><strong>User and Group CRUD</strong> &mdash; admin RPCs, group membership edges</li>
    <li><strong>Audit log</strong> &mdash; every security event written to EntDB</li>
    <li><strong>Admin help requests</strong> &mdash; users who can't log in raise tickets, admins resolve them</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Shape of the service</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code>┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Your apps  ─── Bearer JWT ─►  Downstream services         │
│      │                            │                         │
│      │  Connect-RPC / HTTP        │  verify via JWKS        │
│      ▼                            ▼                         │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐               │
│  │        identity (this service)           │               │
│  │  • signs JWTs (RS256, key ring)          │               │
│  │  • password / passkey / TOTP / OAuth     │               │
│  │  • sessions, audit, user CRUD            │               │
│  │  • /.well-known/jwks.json (port 80)      │               │
│  │  • /metrics                  (port 9090) │               │
│  └─────────────────┬────────────────────────┘               │
│                    │  gRPC                                  │
│                    ▼                                        │
│              ┌──────────────┐                               │
│              │    EntDB     │  per-tenant graph storage     │
│              └──────────────┘                               │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>

  <h2>Where it fits</h2>
  <p>Identity is one image, deployed once per product. It treats EntDB as its data plane &mdash; users, groups, sessions, refresh tokens, passkeys, TOTP secrets, and audit events all live in EntDB nodes (type IDs <code>1&ndash;99</code>). Other services consuming the same EntDB instance use type IDs <code>100+</code> to avoid collisions.</p>

